WEBVTT

00:14.222 --> 00:17.225
Please wait for the game to commence.

00:17.308 --> 00:20.437
Five minutes until registration closes.

00:22.480 --> 00:24.482
It's a Ferris wheel this time?

00:26.568 --> 00:28.528
What game could it be?

00:30.864 --> 00:33.033
Our visas are expiring tonight.

00:36.077 --> 00:37.245
We have no choice but to join.

00:39.497 --> 00:40.874
Do you guys have a minute?

00:43.668 --> 00:47.172
Have you ever heard of "the Beach"?

00:47.756 --> 00:48.590
What?

00:49.257 --> 00:50.925
- Ignore him. Let's go!
- Wait!

01:06.566 --> 01:08.777
Just where is the Beach?

01:09.611 --> 01:11.529
Registration has closed.

02:26.271 --> 02:28.815
We can't seem to find the Beach anywhere.

02:30.024 --> 02:32.485
We are back here again.

02:39.993 --> 02:42.829
If we don't participate in a game soon,
our visas will expire.

02:53.423 --> 02:55.258
My visa will only last
for another three days.

03:02.223 --> 03:03.391
I have three days

03:04.976 --> 03:06.853
to find out where the Beach is

03:08.229 --> 03:10.273
and put an end to this ridiculous game.

03:18.907 --> 03:21.701
Are you really going to hunt with me
in the morning?

03:22.911 --> 03:23.828
Is that all right?

03:24.579 --> 03:26.831
I'll try my best not to stand in your way.

03:28.917 --> 03:31.920
What you've learned
while living in nature,

03:32.879 --> 03:35.215
I want to pick up those skills too
while there's still time.

03:38.092 --> 03:39.844
There's a limit to our lives.

03:41.721 --> 03:44.140
I've lived my life so far
without thinking about that.

03:47.143 --> 03:48.436
Those guys.

03:49.437 --> 03:51.105
They died believing in me.

03:53.608 --> 03:55.902
I may also die in the near future.

03:57.612 --> 03:58.821
For now,

04:00.198 --> 04:02.867
I don't want to waste
even a single minute or second!

04:08.498 --> 04:09.332
Good night.

04:38.778 --> 04:40.905
When there are no lights in the city,

04:42.323 --> 04:43.950
the stars look really beautiful.

04:58.256 --> 04:59.299
That hurts!

05:01.426 --> 05:02.343
Itchy.

05:03.469 --> 05:04.554
It's so itchy.

05:08.391 --> 05:10.935
That's why I told you
it's impossible to sleep outside.

05:12.270 --> 05:14.397
Just come inside the tent already.

05:15.064 --> 05:15.940
What?

05:16.441 --> 05:17.692
But…

05:20.820 --> 05:22.822
It's important to have sufficient sleep.

05:23.364 --> 05:27.160
If you can't even take care of yourself,
you might die anytime here.

05:59.901 --> 06:00.902
This is a mud puddle.

06:02.111 --> 06:04.364
Boars clean themselves here.

06:04.906 --> 06:05.907
What's more,

06:07.241 --> 06:09.827
you can see the ground they dug
to eat leaf buds

06:10.578 --> 06:12.955
as well as the marks they left
while sharpening their fangs.

06:13.831 --> 06:15.291
There are boars in Odaiba?

06:16.626 --> 06:19.921
There's no one left in the cities,
so the animals came in.

06:23.299 --> 06:25.802
Looking at footprints
is a basic hunting technique.

06:27.387 --> 06:31.224
The habitat of beasts
expands out like mesh.

06:33.476 --> 06:36.479
What you need in hunting
is the ability to connect these mesh lines

06:37.063 --> 06:39.732
and understand
the movements of these animals.

06:41.025 --> 06:45.780
So we shouldn't just focus on one thing.
We need to consider the big picture.

06:46.697 --> 06:50.535
- You learn fast.
- I fought the same way in Battleland.

06:51.327 --> 06:52.286
Battleland?

06:53.204 --> 06:54.288
Oh, it's an online game.

06:55.248 --> 06:56.165
Online game?

06:56.958 --> 06:58.084
Games you play online.

07:16.394 --> 07:17.311
How is it?

07:19.147 --> 07:21.023
There are
around ten participants, I think.

07:22.275 --> 07:24.193
There are some who have formed teams, too.

07:24.819 --> 07:25.862
What about your side?

07:25.945 --> 07:29.198
There are four people here.
I'll talk to them and pretend I'm joining.

07:30.450 --> 07:31.451
Wait, Usagi!

07:32.869 --> 07:35.288
- What's the matter?
- Look at the participants' wrists.

07:35.872 --> 07:38.207
- Wrists?
- Is there anyone wearing a locker key?

07:39.000 --> 07:40.918
The ones that you usually see in gyms.

07:43.171 --> 07:45.047
If I remember, during our tag game…

07:45.840 --> 07:46.841
I got it.

07:51.637 --> 07:53.347
Those with the keys are a team.

07:54.098 --> 07:55.475
From where I'm standing,

07:57.268 --> 07:58.436
there are two of them!

07:58.519 --> 08:00.146
Take note of those two.

08:01.063 --> 08:01.898
Understood.

08:12.617 --> 08:14.327
Those who cleared the game
left the building.

08:14.410 --> 08:16.496
I knew it!
They're all wearing locker keys.

08:16.579 --> 08:19.540
There are three people left in my area.
They are leaving.

08:19.624 --> 08:21.792
The two with the locker keys
seem to be a pair.

08:21.876 --> 08:24.045
They're going back to the same area.
I'll follow them!

08:25.796 --> 08:28.257
All right, we did it!

08:28.341 --> 08:31.302
Let's head back!

08:39.352 --> 08:40.186
Usagi.

08:40.978 --> 08:42.188
Do you see it too, Arisu?

08:42.688 --> 08:44.148
I'm sure of it. It's those guys!

08:49.737 --> 08:50.780
There's a car.

08:51.697 --> 08:54.951
They may be collecting these cars
systematically.

08:57.078 --> 08:58.329
They're on the move!

08:58.412 --> 08:59.830
Same over here!

09:05.545 --> 09:07.088
The car is moving towards Maihama!

09:07.588 --> 09:08.506
This side, too!

09:44.917 --> 09:46.002
Is that the place?

09:52.508 --> 09:53.509
BEACH

09:53.593 --> 09:54.594
"The Beach."

09:56.137 --> 09:57.054
That's the place!

09:57.972 --> 09:59.515
How do they have electricity?

10:01.475 --> 10:03.853
Will we find the answers
to our questions there?

10:19.160 --> 10:20.369
Good morning.

10:21.412 --> 10:23.706
I'm sorry that we were so rough.

10:24.457 --> 10:27.668
We heard that there were some people
sneaking around the place.

10:28.753 --> 10:30.296
What are your motives?

10:34.800 --> 10:38.220
We heard that we'll know the answer…
if we come here.

10:39.889 --> 10:41.557
What this game is about

10:43.017 --> 10:44.769
and where all the people
who disappeared went.

10:49.815 --> 10:51.150
Exactly.

10:52.610 --> 10:55.696
We know the answers
to the questions you both have.

11:02.244 --> 11:03.496
Welcome

11:04.955 --> 11:07.750
to the Beach, the utopia.

11:15.174 --> 11:16.425
This…

11:16.509 --> 11:17.802
is the answer.

11:51.252 --> 11:53.045
I'll tell you the truth.

11:54.630 --> 11:59.844
There's only one way
to end this hellish nightmare.

12:00.761 --> 12:05.349
We clear the games
and collect all the playing cards.

12:07.435 --> 12:09.186
All the playing cards?

12:10.896 --> 12:12.481
So if we gather all of them,

12:13.315 --> 12:15.526
will the original world return?

12:19.822 --> 12:21.490
The original world will not return.

12:22.867 --> 12:24.535
Only one person

12:25.119 --> 12:27.413
can return to the original world.

12:30.791 --> 12:31.709
Only one person?

12:34.545 --> 12:37.047
It's impossible for a single person

12:37.131 --> 12:39.884
to clear all the games
and gather all 52 playing cards.

12:40.593 --> 12:42.636
You can't leave this country
by working alone.

12:43.471 --> 12:47.808
That's why everyone unites as one

12:48.601 --> 12:50.686
in order to let that one person
leave the country.

12:51.729 --> 12:54.106
This is the Beach's objective.

12:55.399 --> 13:00.404
I've heard that the two of you
possess good cards.

13:01.197 --> 13:07.620
I'll have both of you play your part
and help us gather the remaining cards.

13:10.164 --> 13:11.290
And if we refuse?

13:11.373 --> 13:14.168
You can't reject me.

13:15.920 --> 13:19.840
Your visa is expiring today.

13:22.092 --> 13:24.595
You have no choice
but to participate in a game, don't you?

13:27.181 --> 13:29.266
We can return if we gather all the cards.

13:30.976 --> 13:32.186
Is that really true?

13:33.229 --> 13:34.855
I can't reveal everything yet,

13:35.648 --> 13:38.317
but I have a credible source
for that information.

13:40.236 --> 13:44.698
Before both of you entered this world,
we already thoroughly investigated

13:45.324 --> 13:47.201
everything about this country.

13:48.410 --> 13:51.497
You've been referring to this place
as a "country."

13:52.414 --> 13:56.168
The fact that we've been issued visas

13:57.044 --> 13:58.504
means that this is a country.

14:00.923 --> 14:04.552
The people in Tokyo didn't just disappear.

14:05.344 --> 14:10.474
It's hypothesized that we've entered
another country accidentally.

14:11.308 --> 14:15.437
If that's true,
then there must be a way to return.

14:16.605 --> 14:21.735
And we created an organization here.

14:21.819 --> 14:27.908
Fuels are used to generate electricity,
and rainwater is used as a water supply.

14:28.492 --> 14:31.328
We have even secured firearms
around the country.

14:32.329 --> 14:36.667
However, only a selected few
are allowed to use them.

14:37.960 --> 14:42.047
Our objective is to unite
and collect all the playing cards.

14:43.257 --> 14:44.550
And…

14:45.175 --> 14:49.638
there are only three rules
in this utopian Beach.

14:50.806 --> 14:55.060
Rule number one. You must
always wear swimsuits at the Beach.

14:56.395 --> 14:57.229
What?

14:58.856 --> 15:02.860
You can't hide firearms in a swimsuit.
Safe, isn't it?

15:03.903 --> 15:10.701
You're free to drink,
take drugs, or even have sex!

15:11.994 --> 15:15.205
Feel free
to enjoy your life to the fullest.

15:16.123 --> 15:20.169
We damaged all the door locks
with super glue.

15:20.252 --> 15:21.837
No one is allowed to hide anything!

15:23.172 --> 15:24.381
Rule number two.

15:25.090 --> 15:28.260
All playing cards belong to the Beach.

15:28.928 --> 15:34.934
We will take away all the cards
the two of you possess.

15:37.478 --> 15:41.649
Those that have contributed more cards
will be promoted to a higher number.

15:42.566 --> 15:47.279
After everyone works together
to get the first person out the country,

15:47.947 --> 15:50.824
if we gather enough duplicated cards,

15:50.908 --> 15:53.202
we will soon be able to have the second

15:53.285 --> 15:55.371
or even the third person
to leave this country.

15:56.997 --> 16:02.378
The day will come when everyone
at the Beach will be able to leave!

16:05.839 --> 16:07.841
And when will that be?

16:11.762 --> 16:12.805
What if…

16:14.223 --> 16:15.474
I reject your offer?

16:26.527 --> 16:28.487
Rule number three of the Beach.

16:30.739 --> 16:32.449
This is the last rule.

16:35.953 --> 16:38.414
Death to the traitors.

16:46.588 --> 16:49.425
Everyone at the Beach vowed

16:49.508 --> 16:52.386
to produce the first departure
from this country

16:52.469 --> 16:54.221
at the cost of our lives.

16:54.304 --> 16:57.224
It's our mission, our duty!

17:00.769 --> 17:03.230
Those who show contempt for that…

17:04.398 --> 17:06.650
will never be forgiven by the Beach.

17:28.380 --> 17:29.465
Usagi.

17:30.758 --> 17:31.633
I'm sorry.

17:33.510 --> 17:35.095
I dragged you into this.

17:38.015 --> 17:39.224
Don't apologize.

17:40.851 --> 17:42.394
I wasn't dragged into this.

17:44.855 --> 17:46.607
This is a path that I chose.

18:14.968 --> 18:16.553
It's the Seven of Hearts!

18:17.596 --> 18:19.598
Luck is on our side.

18:21.016 --> 18:24.353
Now we're another step closer
to departure!

18:24.436 --> 18:25.604
Thank you!

18:26.980 --> 18:31.318
We will consider promoting both of you
to a higher rank number.

18:32.486 --> 18:37.449
Well then,
please enjoy your stay at the Beach!

19:09.189 --> 19:10.691
What the hell is this?

19:41.513 --> 19:42.514
Somehow,

19:43.390 --> 19:45.017
it feels like we're being watched.

19:46.602 --> 19:48.562
Newcomers are always
a spectacle to others.

20:01.241 --> 20:07.456
This is the Beach's Special Time!

20:10.834 --> 20:11.919
This is completely

20:12.419 --> 20:13.837
an escape from reality.

20:16.173 --> 20:18.592
It's time for the games!

20:23.639 --> 20:27.893
A new game arena
has been located in the Shinagawa ward!

20:27.976 --> 20:32.481
- The cars are in the second parking lot!
- Adachi and Koto wards, form two groups!

20:32.564 --> 20:38.362
- Hatter!
- Hatter!

20:49.248 --> 20:50.582
My comrades!

20:51.250 --> 20:53.252
The time has come again tonight.

20:54.878 --> 20:56.755
Do not falter!

20:57.339 --> 21:01.093
This is a war against fear!

21:01.927 --> 21:05.472
Everyone here has the courage
to overcome their obstacles.

21:06.181 --> 21:08.100
Everyone here

21:08.976 --> 21:10.769
is now one!

21:12.396 --> 21:15.315
We shall unite and gather all cards

21:16.066 --> 21:18.110
and return to the original world together!

21:19.278 --> 21:20.112
And…

21:20.779 --> 21:22.322
that day is upon us!

21:24.825 --> 21:25.993
Let's go!

21:29.621 --> 21:31.915
Get in the car marked with your number!

21:33.792 --> 21:36.920
So we're just an army
to collect the cards, huh?

21:38.088 --> 21:39.798
We've been divided into separate games.

21:41.091 --> 21:42.384
You must survive.

21:47.973 --> 21:49.099
What's the matter?

21:50.767 --> 21:52.644
I was in the same game as them.

21:54.354 --> 21:55.689
The two of them?

21:55.772 --> 21:56.732
Yes.

21:57.733 --> 21:59.109
They might be useful.

21:59.609 --> 22:01.111
To our plan, that is.

22:07.617 --> 22:10.537
Teams 1 to 9 will head
to the Shinagawa ward,

22:10.620 --> 22:13.415
while Teams 10 to 17
will head to the Koto ward.

22:13.498 --> 22:15.292
Teams 18 to 24 will…

22:15.375 --> 22:17.627
Game, "Beast Hunter."

22:18.211 --> 22:21.631
Using this scoreboard as a reference,

22:21.715 --> 22:24.926
please cooperate and defeat
the beasts in the area together.

22:36.980 --> 22:38.899
Game, "Hunting Competition."

22:44.738 --> 22:47.157
Game, "Human Elevator."

22:52.245 --> 22:54.915
Game, "Bingo in Match Factory."

22:56.958 --> 22:59.086
You only have nine matches.

22:59.586 --> 23:03.840
Answer all the numbers
you find across the 24 rooms

23:03.924 --> 23:05.759
and clear the game by achieving bingo.

23:08.929 --> 23:10.180
It's the militants!

23:12.057 --> 23:13.350
50 POINTS RECEIVED

23:13.433 --> 23:14.643
30 POINTS RECEIVED

23:19.731 --> 23:21.691
Just where the hell is it?

23:52.097 --> 23:53.598
Where is it hiding?

24:08.780 --> 24:09.948
ONE POINT RECEIVED

24:10.031 --> 24:11.741
Piece of cake!

24:14.286 --> 24:15.537
Here it is!

24:16.288 --> 24:17.539
Room 4D is nine!

24:17.622 --> 24:19.541
PLAYERS

25:10.884 --> 25:14.846
ONE PER PERSON

25:19.893 --> 25:23.939
This is a trial to see if you're fit to be
an executive member of Beach.

25:24.814 --> 25:26.149
Well, do your best.

25:32.489 --> 25:34.157
A waterproof case?

25:36.785 --> 25:39.287
I'm Kuina. Nice to meet you.

25:41.164 --> 25:42.249
Nice to meet you.

25:43.291 --> 25:44.292
Ann!

25:44.876 --> 25:47.212
Water is starting to spurt out,
and it's filling up the area!

25:48.255 --> 25:50.590
Hey, you're…

25:51.883 --> 25:55.512
You're the one from the tag game.
So you're alive.

25:56.096 --> 25:58.181
Yes, I help with maintenance
at the Beach and--

25:58.265 --> 26:00.183
Leave the formalities for after the game.

26:23.582 --> 26:25.000
What's with this room?

26:28.670 --> 26:30.589
Registration has closed.

26:31.089 --> 26:33.341
There are currently seven participants.

26:33.925 --> 26:35.552
The game will now commence.

26:37.679 --> 26:40.348
Difficulty, Four of Diamonds.

26:41.057 --> 26:43.435
The last Diamond card we need.

26:44.978 --> 26:47.772
Game, "Light Bulb."

26:48.857 --> 26:49.733
"Light bulb"?

26:50.567 --> 26:52.402
OPEN AND CLOSE FREELY

26:56.448 --> 26:57.449
Question.

26:58.033 --> 27:00.660
Which switch turns on the light bulb?

27:03.705 --> 27:05.582
WHICH SWITCH TURNS ON THE LIGHT BULB?

27:05.665 --> 27:07.000
Rule number one.

27:08.168 --> 27:14.549
Only one switch among A, B, and C
will turn on the light bulb.

27:15.842 --> 27:17.010
Rule number two.

27:19.262 --> 27:21.222
You only have one chance

27:21.306 --> 27:24.267
to flip a switch while the door is open.

27:26.895 --> 27:27.729
OPEN AND CLOSE FREELY

27:27.812 --> 27:31.983
If the door is closed, you can flip
the switches as much as you like.

27:35.111 --> 27:36.112
Rule number three.

27:37.572 --> 27:43.203
If someone is in the room,
or if a switch has been turned on,

27:44.162 --> 27:46.956
the door will be locked in place
and cannot be moved.

27:49.542 --> 27:52.545
You only have one chance
to answer as a group.

27:53.588 --> 27:56.883
If you answer correctly
which switch turns on the light bulb,

27:56.966 --> 27:58.051
you clear the game.

27:58.843 --> 28:03.515
If the water level rises and touches
the electrical wires, it's game over.

28:05.058 --> 28:06.267
Electrical wires?

28:12.065 --> 28:14.234
You'll get electrocuted!

28:15.652 --> 28:16.986
Is that what they meant?

28:19.072 --> 28:20.490
The water level is slowly rising!

28:21.074 --> 28:23.034
If it rises too high, everyone dies.

28:23.618 --> 28:26.955
Anyway, we just need to figure out
the switch for the light bulb, right?

28:27.038 --> 28:29.582
I'll head into that room first,
so let's take turns!

28:29.666 --> 28:31.376
If you enter, the door won't close!

28:32.252 --> 28:33.670
Let's see…

28:33.753 --> 28:37.173
So we only have one chance
to turn on the switch with the door open.

28:37.257 --> 28:40.385
But there's no point in flipping
the switches when the door is closed!

28:41.094 --> 28:45.056
For example, if you turn on Switch A
with the door open

28:45.140 --> 28:48.685
and it doesn't light up,
then the answer is not A.

28:49.269 --> 28:51.020
And why is that wrong?

28:53.148 --> 28:56.317
Anyway, let's just flip Switch A
with the door open--

28:56.401 --> 28:58.069
What if your answer is wrong?

28:58.153 --> 29:01.197
If it turns on, it's A.
If it doesn't, it's either B or C.

29:01.281 --> 29:05.243
- At least we have a 50 percent chance!
- It's 66 percent.

29:06.703 --> 29:08.246
Shouldn't it be 50 percent?

29:08.329 --> 29:11.040
I don't understand it at all.

29:11.624 --> 29:13.501
What will you do, Arisu?

29:16.171 --> 29:17.589
But there's no other choice.

29:18.256 --> 29:20.759
For now, let's turn on a switch
with the door open!

29:20.842 --> 29:24.179
If the bulb doesn't turn on,
we'll decide on one out of the two!

29:24.304 --> 29:25.722
Are you just going to guess?

29:26.890 --> 29:29.392
- We have no choice but to bet on it.
- Using all seven lives here?

29:33.480 --> 29:34.647
Or six, I guess.

29:35.565 --> 29:38.443
Yes. If you know the answer,
then do it already!

29:38.526 --> 29:39.944
Didn't I tell you?

29:40.028 --> 29:41.780
I'm testing you.

29:43.323 --> 29:45.992
Don't drag us into the newcomer's trial!

29:46.075 --> 29:47.202
Giving up already?

29:47.285 --> 29:50.288
I give up! Please tell us the answer!

29:52.248 --> 29:54.250
This is really bad!

29:55.251 --> 29:56.461
Ann!

29:57.504 --> 30:00.131
Arisu, just do it.
It's going to be too late!

30:01.299 --> 30:02.258
I'm doing it then!

30:03.635 --> 30:06.346
Are you really all right with that?

30:11.142 --> 30:12.310
Just do it already!

30:12.393 --> 30:13.645
What are you waiting for?

30:22.529 --> 30:24.239
You only have one chance

30:24.322 --> 30:26.324
to flip a switch while the door is open.

30:26.407 --> 30:29.118
For example, if you turn on Switch A
with the door open

30:29.202 --> 30:31.704
and it doesn't light up,
then the answer is not A.

30:31.788 --> 30:34.374
If it turns on, it's A.
If it doesn't, it's either B or C.

30:34.457 --> 30:38.336
If the door is closed, you can flip
the switches as much as you like.

30:39.629 --> 30:41.005
Let's close the door.

30:41.089 --> 30:42.131
What?

30:42.966 --> 30:45.635
Close the door! Hurry up!

30:45.718 --> 30:48.680
If you don't do as Arisu says,
everyone will die!

31:00.984 --> 31:01.943
Stay like this!

31:02.986 --> 31:06.114
- What are you up to?
- I hope you know what you're doing!

31:21.004 --> 31:22.171
Hurry up!

31:24.299 --> 31:25.300
Open the door!

31:35.810 --> 31:37.186
Hurry up.

31:43.109 --> 31:44.527
It didn't turn on!

31:44.611 --> 31:46.821
Kuina, touch the bulb!

31:46.905 --> 31:50.533
- What?
- Just go! We're running out of time.

31:53.953 --> 31:55.830
Please!

31:57.999 --> 31:59.042
That's hot!

31:59.626 --> 32:01.002
- The answer is A--
- Switch A!

32:21.856 --> 32:24.484
Game cleared. Congratulations.

32:33.201 --> 32:34.702
Electricity generates heat.

32:34.786 --> 32:37.205
If the bulb had been on,
it would feel hot.

32:37.288 --> 32:38.915
If not, it would have felt cold.

32:39.499 --> 32:41.918
And we only had one chance
to check with our own eyes.

32:42.502 --> 32:46.255
With this, the chance of survival was
increased from 66 to 100 percent.

32:51.594 --> 32:53.179
It's 50 percent, right?

32:53.888 --> 32:55.473
I don't care anymore.

33:27.296 --> 33:28.172
You survived.

33:29.132 --> 33:29.966
Yes.

33:35.930 --> 33:38.224
She knew the answer.

33:41.227 --> 33:43.813
Ann was trying to test me.

33:45.148 --> 33:47.483
When in Rome, do as the Romans do.

33:52.822 --> 33:53.906
Your girlfriend?

33:53.990 --> 33:54.866
What?

33:55.783 --> 33:56.826
You're wrong!

33:57.410 --> 33:59.704
You guys get along,
so why not date each other?

34:00.455 --> 34:02.874
You never know when you're going to die.

34:02.957 --> 34:04.333
What are you saying?

34:04.417 --> 34:06.669
There are things you should do
while you're still alive!

34:10.381 --> 34:12.717
My mom is sick in the hospital.

34:13.384 --> 34:16.137
She can't even relieve herself
without my help,

34:16.220 --> 34:18.139
and yet I had to be separated from her.

34:19.432 --> 34:21.059
So I want to return alive.

34:22.060 --> 34:24.854
That's why I quit smoking.

34:25.605 --> 34:28.608
I haven't been able to quit before this.

34:29.192 --> 34:31.778
I'll need some stamina
in order to survive, right?

34:33.946 --> 34:36.324
I'll definitely survive
and return to the original world.

34:37.742 --> 34:40.620
Hey, stop playing that tacky music!

34:52.507 --> 34:54.759
It's the militants at the Beach.

34:55.551 --> 34:57.887
If you want
to live peacefully at the Beach,

34:57.970 --> 34:59.889
avoid getting involved with them.

35:03.559 --> 35:05.978
The leader, Aguni, is an ex-SDF officer,

35:06.062 --> 35:09.065
and he is in charge of
all the weapons at the Beach.

35:10.483 --> 35:12.944
The ones currently in power at the Beach

35:13.027 --> 35:16.364
are the Number One, Hatter,
and his devotees

35:17.281 --> 35:19.450
as well as the militants led by Aguni.

35:21.077 --> 35:24.038
We've only barely managed
to maintain peace and order here,

35:24.122 --> 35:27.834
but a conflict between the two parties
could happen anytime.

35:37.969 --> 35:39.428
What happened to your pal?

35:46.394 --> 35:48.146
I see. He died.

35:49.522 --> 35:50.481
What a shame.

35:51.315 --> 35:53.359
So only the small fish survived.

35:54.569 --> 35:55.820
Do you know each other?

36:01.492 --> 36:02.577
You,

36:03.244 --> 36:04.620
bring that woman over.

36:05.246 --> 36:06.080
Yes.

36:07.790 --> 36:10.001
- Hey!
- Stop. Don't get yourself involved!

36:10.918 --> 36:13.546
Our boss says
he wants to have a taste of you.

36:15.590 --> 36:16.799
Come.

36:17.383 --> 36:18.593
Stop it.

36:20.178 --> 36:22.972
What should we do about this kid?

36:23.556 --> 36:26.267
Break his legs
so that he'll die in the next game.

36:27.101 --> 36:28.519
Yes. You guys!

36:29.103 --> 36:30.271
Bring the woman to him.

36:31.272 --> 36:32.690
You come with me.

36:34.150 --> 36:35.359
Stand up.

36:45.286 --> 36:46.662
Is this a fight?

36:52.376 --> 36:55.379
Back off, Hatter.
This doesn't concern you.

36:57.048 --> 36:59.091
I can't do that.

36:59.926 --> 37:03.763
As the Number One, I'm obliged
to maintain order at the Beach.

37:06.474 --> 37:13.314
Could you let off the newcomers
on my account, Aguni?

37:21.405 --> 37:22.448
Niragi.

37:24.784 --> 37:27.912
I only take orders from the boss.

37:36.963 --> 37:39.548
Then let me ask your boss.

37:43.594 --> 37:46.013
Who is your boss,

37:46.639 --> 37:47.765
Aguni?

38:03.614 --> 38:05.199
It's you, right?

38:13.416 --> 38:15.209
Go take a shower.

38:16.002 --> 38:18.796
All executive members are to gather
in the meeting room!

38:25.428 --> 38:27.847
Arisu, you're coming too.

38:29.807 --> 38:32.268
I've heard about your potential from Ann.

38:33.686 --> 38:34.645
Follow me.

38:42.945 --> 38:43.779
I'll be back.

38:58.085 --> 39:01.505
So what do you think about him?

39:03.674 --> 39:04.967
I like him.

39:06.093 --> 39:09.347
- We still have four missing.
- We're starting the meeting!

39:09.430 --> 39:11.515
Those who have nothing to do here, leave.

39:33.287 --> 39:34.288
It's you.

39:35.581 --> 39:37.041
Two of Spades.

39:38.209 --> 39:41.212
Six of Spades. Four of Diamonds.

39:41.712 --> 39:43.798
Two of Clubs.
We've collected all four of them.

39:45.091 --> 39:49.345
Until now, we still haven't found
any face cards.

39:50.429 --> 39:53.891
If face cards do not exist,
then we're only left with Ten of Hearts.

39:55.768 --> 39:56.769
Ten of Hearts.

39:57.645 --> 40:00.147
It has never appeared in a game before.

40:05.486 --> 40:07.488
If it doesn't appear, we can't clear it.

40:08.072 --> 40:10.449
Maybe there needs
to be a condition for it to appear.

40:11.700 --> 40:12.993
Maybe it is not in Tokyo.

40:13.911 --> 40:16.539
A game arena has never been found
outside of Tokyo.

40:16.622 --> 40:20.584
- But we haven't investigated that far yet.
- The strategy won't change.

40:22.711 --> 40:25.423
We will continue investigating
the game arenas in town.

40:26.173 --> 40:29.885
Make sure you have days left on your visas
and keep a lookout for the Ten of Hearts.

40:31.679 --> 40:34.306
I need to replenish my visa soon.

40:41.897 --> 40:46.360
There's a way to earn visa days for sure.

40:47.361 --> 40:48.237
Is that so?

40:50.489 --> 40:55.703
Heart games let you toy
with the hearts and feelings of others.

40:57.204 --> 40:59.623
If you bring along those
that don't mind dying,

41:00.207 --> 41:02.585
you'll survive for sure.

41:05.254 --> 41:08.257
Even in the Seven of Hearts game
that Arisu cleared.

41:09.175 --> 41:10.718
The same thing happened, didn't it?

41:11.635 --> 41:14.763
It's a game that doesn't
even require you to use your brain!

41:16.807 --> 41:18.934
As someone who cleared a Hearts game,

41:19.435 --> 41:21.312
do you have any advice for us, Arisu?

41:26.484 --> 41:29.695
But would a Hearts game
appear so conveniently?

41:30.196 --> 41:35.117
On top of that, we won't know what type
of game it is until registration closes.

41:35.201 --> 41:38.704
But we should be able to deduce it
based on the probability theory.

41:40.372 --> 41:43.375
I don't need
such a pretentious investigation method.

41:44.793 --> 41:46.879
I'll join the next game.

41:47.421 --> 41:49.590
Be it Hearts or Spades.

41:50.132 --> 41:52.801
Someone like me with a 100 percent
winning rate will clear it easily!

41:53.594 --> 41:56.222
I'll join the games
until the Ten of Hearts card appears!

41:57.139 --> 42:00.518
The day where we gather all cards
and depart from this country is near!

42:02.811 --> 42:06.649
Executive members, I'm counting on
you guys to oversee things here.

42:09.735 --> 42:11.111
The meeting is adjourned!

42:58.033 --> 43:00.202
You should drink too, Arisu.

43:05.374 --> 43:09.628
I also like to enjoy myself before a game.

43:18.387 --> 43:20.973
There's no poison in it!

43:30.065 --> 43:34.445
It seems like you don't trust me.

43:39.074 --> 43:42.745
I like your prudence.

43:44.455 --> 43:46.415
What did you do in the original world?

43:49.043 --> 43:50.127
Nothing.

43:51.629 --> 43:52.588
So you're a NEET?

43:55.007 --> 43:59.720
I ran a host club in Kabukicho.

44:00.846 --> 44:02.014
It's called Beach.

44:02.848 --> 44:03.932
Have you heard of it?

44:07.519 --> 44:09.563
It was quite famous, you know?

44:09.647 --> 44:14.860
Beach, Beach, there's no sand
But it's the utopia Beach

44:18.530 --> 44:21.367
It was advertised all over Tokyo
on cars with loudspeakers, you know?

44:22.743 --> 44:24.036
All I did was play games at home.

44:34.421 --> 44:35.547
Did you know?

44:38.550 --> 44:41.095
I wanted to be the best in Kabukicho…

44:43.138 --> 44:45.349
desperately.

44:54.400 --> 44:56.819
My subordinates all looked up to me,

44:58.320 --> 45:01.281
and I told them I'll do
whatever it takes to rule over this place!

45:08.372 --> 45:09.748
As a host,

45:11.959 --> 45:14.503
it's all over if you're looked down on
by your customers.

45:16.463 --> 45:18.632
No matter how much you're made to drink…

45:20.843 --> 45:25.389
you must never lose your human pride.

45:27.725 --> 45:30.644
I instilled that mindset
into my subordinates.

45:35.315 --> 45:36.358
However…

45:41.155 --> 45:43.615
that pushed him over the edge.

45:48.370 --> 45:49.413
In the dormitory,

45:53.459 --> 45:54.960
he hanged himself.

45:59.882 --> 46:00.966
Everyone.

46:04.553 --> 46:06.597
They all left me.

46:11.727 --> 46:12.936
I…

46:16.774 --> 46:19.401
I wanted to rule the place with them.

46:26.909 --> 46:28.619
Now that I think about it,

46:31.246 --> 46:34.082
his death was a necessary evil.

46:37.211 --> 46:39.630
In order for me to mature.

46:42.007 --> 46:43.383
Mature?

46:47.387 --> 46:49.598
In this new Beach,

46:50.516 --> 46:55.938
all the players will devote
their bodies and lives to me!

46:58.816 --> 47:01.318
And I will be a hero.

47:04.488 --> 47:07.658
The one and only hero

47:07.741 --> 47:09.993
to succeed in leaving this country!

47:14.081 --> 47:16.166
And that is me, Hatter.

47:32.766 --> 47:34.434
For a hero,

47:35.769 --> 47:37.688
tragedies are needed.

47:46.822 --> 47:48.532
To the second Beach.

50:44.583 --> 50:47.627
Subtitle translation by: Qianni Lu
